  "reason": "Existing evidence shows multiprofile RNA with scvi is the strongest direction (0.650-0.653 validation accuracy), and avgpool is the more reliable aggregation: it is clearly better for PCA and nearly tied for scvi. scgpt is an untested RNA representation. This experiment tests whether scgpt improves over scvi while holding profile setting and aggregation constant, isolating the effect of representation. It is the best next use of budget because it has high expected performance, directly extends the strongest RNA-only evidence, and avoids relying on the small transformer advantage or jumping to a confounded multimodal fusion test before establishing the best RNA encoder."
}

